-- title:
--   Kronecker remainder equals q⁻¹(j_q-j^q)(j-j_q^{ q})
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (an algebraic closure of $\mathbb Q$). Let `data` be a `ModularPolynomialData q`, that is, a polynomial $\Phi \in \mathbb Z[x][Y]$ which is monic, has degree $\psi(q)=\sum_{d\mid q,\ d\text{ squarefree}} q/d$ in $Y$, and satisfies $\Phi=0$ when the inner variable $x$ is sent to the $q$-expansion $j\in\mathbb Q((\mathsf q))$ and the outer variable $Y$ to $j_q$, the image of $j$ under the substitution $\mathsf q\mapsto \mathsf q^{q}$ on Laurent series. Let $R \in \mathbb Z[x][Y]$ satisfy the Kronecker decomposition $\Phi = (x^{q}-Y)(x-Y^{q}) + qR$. Transport $R$ to a two-variable polynomial over $A$, with $x\mapsto X_0$ and $Y\mapsto X_1$, and evaluate it by `NodeLocalized.modularEval (1 * q) A.toSubring`, which maps $A$ into $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ by the constant-series embedding, $X_0$ to the series $j$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $X_1$ to its substitution $\mathsf q\mapsto\mathsf q^{1\cdot q}$. The assertion is the identity $$R(j,j_q) = q^{-1}\,(j_q - j^{q})\,(j - j_q^{\,q})$$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$, where $j$ and $j_q$ on the right are the coefficientwise images of the rational series $j$ and $j_q$, regarded as elements of the compositum $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ generated by the image of the full modular function field of level $1\cdot q$, and $q^{-1}$ is the inverse of the constant series $q$.
--
--   This is the Laurent-series form of Kronecker's congruence $\Phi_q \equiv (x^{q}-Y)(x-Y^{q}) \pmod q$: it expresses the remainder term $R$ of that congruence, evaluated at the two standard generators $j$, $j_q$ of the modular function field of level $q$, as the explicit product $q^{-1}(j_q-j^q)(j-j_q^{\,q})$. It is the dictionary that makes the local equation $GH = qU$ available inside the node rings, and is used by the lemmas producing two-branch normalisations at the singular points of the reduction of $X_0(q)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_modularEval_kroneckerRemainder.lean

